# THIS REPO MUST STAY PRIVATE.
# It contains her phone number, email, CV content and case-study notes. Nothing
# here is secret-scanner protected — privacy comes from the repo being private.
# Never make it public, never fork it to a public org.

# Real secrets never get committed. Keys live in ~/.job-agent.env locally and in
# GitHub Actions secrets in CI.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Local tooling
.venv-tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Transient per-run files — regenerated every run, no value in history
db/jobs_new.jsonl
db/digest.md
db/needs_browser.txt
db/local_cron.log
db/launchd.daily.log
db/launchd.approvals.log

# Telegram poll cursor and the approval queue are state, and MUST be committed
# or a 'send' command replays and mails twice. Listed here only as a reminder
# that they are intentional:
#   db/pending.json
#   db/tg_offset.json
.job-agent-state.json

# Committed on purpose (do not add these to the ignore list):
#   profile/            her verified profile and case-study notes
#   targets/            company lists and search config
#   db/jobs.jsonl       what we've already seen, so nothing is notified twice
#   db/scored.jsonl     scoring verdicts
#   db/applied.json     what was prepared, sent, and which follow-ups are due
#   out/                tailored resumes and drafted emails, needed for follow-ups
